<article class="env-definition" id="C48C3A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/C48C3A">Definition <span data-tag="C48C3A">2.3.3.1</span>.</a>minimal!inner fibration Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be an inner fibration of simplicial sets. We will say that $p$ is <em>minimal</em> if $f=f'$ for every pair of maps $f,f': \Delta ^ n \rightarrow X$ which are homotopic relative to $\bd \Delta ^ n$ over $S$. </p>
  <p>We will say that an $\infty $-category $\calC $ is <em>minimal</em> if the associated inner fibration $\calC \rightarrow \ast $ is minimal.minimal!$\infty $-category </p>
